From 2c797321b53e1c86da56bf2fb18e0840dddfd0b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Sisong 2.16-5 and clangd_server: completion in the editor

Sisong 2.16-5 (ProseApps 831c322) gains Edit > Complete Word: the word
before the caret completed from an index of the Be/Haiku API that the
package installs as data/sisong/api-index, and, for C and C++, from
clangd through clangd_server, whose diagnostics show in the editor's
message pane. It also gains a choice of fixed font in its preferences.

clangd_server is new: Prose's BeOS shape around clangd, which speaks
the Language Server Protocol over its own stdin and stdout. It installs
among the system's servers with its signature registered, and Sisong
starts it on the first question from a C or C++ document.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0096-sisong-2-16-5-and-clangd-server-completion-in-the-editor.patch 9bbeae0d934f699efbb2921d61a24a83ee7105904b60588899bed9d3e7a5f072
